{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261103T014645Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "c47704bbd72755ccacc02ff5", "title": "Building AI for Lawyers - Jacob Lauritzen, CTO of Legora", "url": "https://latent.space/p/building-ai-for-lawyers-jacob-lauritzen-cto-of-legora/", "source": "Latent Space", "published": "2026-11-02T23:01:02+00:00", "is_ai": 0.98, "worthiness": 0.765, "worthiness_confidence": 0.89, "final_score": 0.765, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "feed_full_text", "text_chars": 94587, "delivered": true, "summary": "Legora, a legal AI platform, announced a $550M Series E at $8.8B valuation with over $200M ARR and 1,800+ customers. The company built specialized evaluation infrastructure using simulated legal environments since customer data is confidential, employs 100 legal engineers (lawyers with CS backgrounds), and developed core primitives like Tabular Review for bulk document analysis and Lists for workflow orchestration. For AI builders, the key insight is that domain-specific constraints—privacy, compliance, infrastructure choices—drive architectural decisions more than raw model capability, and that 60% of legal work is already solvable with current models, making the focus cost, latency, and orchestration rather than model improvements.", "jev_ms": 325.1, "jev_input_tokens": 20247, "jev_cost": 0.000850374, "llm_ms": 2958.7, "llm_cost": 0.016161, "errors": []}
{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261103T014645Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "de3d36c3550a73257e465c10", "title": "Building Legal Agents When You Can't See the Data - Jacob Lauritzen, CTO of Legora", "url": "https://latent.space/p/building_legal_agents_when_you_can_t_see_the_data_-_jacob_lauritzen_cto_of_legora/", "source": "Latent Space", "published": "2026-11-02T22:54:03+00:00", "is_ai": 0.98, "worthiness": 0.785, "worthiness_confidence": 0.83, "final_score": 0.785, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "feed_full_text", "text_chars": 4970, "delivered": true, "summary": "Legora built a legal AI agent without accessing client data, solving privacy constraints through simulated test environments modeled on customer workflows. The company estimates current models handle 60% of legal work well, with smarter models needed for complex tasks like contract drafting, which Legora frames as a search problem. Key insight: one citation system release improved accuracy from 70% to 99% without model changes, demonstrating that evaluation infrastructure and product design matter as much as model capability for specialized domains.", "jev_ms": 245.8, "jev_input_tokens": 1959, "jev_cost": 8.2278e-05, "llm_ms": 2098.7, "llm_cost": 0.002091, "errors": []}
